"Design exploration (2026-08-10). REJECTED ALTERNATIVE: an explicit battle mode (server-flagged encounter state) -- it forces the filtered-out problem (pros 3/4 die), adds state to sync, and breeds edge cases (fleeing, late joiners, multi-party). PROPOSED MECHANISMS, all within the single system: (1) THREAT is a derived predicate, never stored: hostiles-co-located(player), computable client-side from subscribed location/allegiance/hp tables and equally computable server-side if narration/rules ever need it. No mode row, nothing to desync. (2) DEMOTE, NEVER REMOVE: target list renders as a primary group + a collapsed-but-always-reachable surroundings group; under threat the primary group is hostiles (danger-sorted) and everything else demotes to surroundings; calm relaxes to today's prominence order. Same for actions: validity filtering stays (getActionOptions), threat only re-sorts attack-valid actions to the front. This one rule satisfies cons 1-2 and preserves pros 3-4. (3) FOCUS + ONE-INPUT ATTACK: client keeps a focus target -- auto-focused when exactly one hostile, cycled (e.g. tab) otherwise; one hotkey performs default-attack-on-focus. Server untouched (act(action, target) is already atomic). Considered and deferred: auto-repeat queued attacks (erodes agency). (4) CREATIVE OBJECTS: interactables are ordinary entities with interaction components + a future Activate action type, riding the same act pipeline/tick machinery; reachable in battle via the surroundings group by construction. (5) BREAKABLE SCENERY: decorations optionally get hp + an on-break effect hook (reveal path / spawn item / drop concealment); ordinary attack targets while calm, demoted under threat. (6) PROMINENCE EVOLUTION: server prominence stays static intrinsic notability (note: path bit 1<<8 currently outranks hp 1<<6 -- right for calm, wrong under threat); the threat-aware order is a client-side composition sortKey(prominence, isHostile, threat). FIRST SLICE (UI-only, no server change): threat predicate + demote-not-remove grouping + single-hostile auto-focus + attack-focus hotkey. SECOND SLICE (content+server): breakable decorations with on-break reveals; Activate-type interactions after that."